@Steve L 

I think young people have no idea in general how different television viewing was back in the day. Each show had its night and you had to be home to watch your favorites. If you missed it, you had to wait for the reruns which is why most shows were episodic. And when there was the occasional “two-parter”’ you definitely had to be home. Also there were 24 episodes in a season, so every episode didn’t have to be “an event”. You might laugh at the original series of Star Trek back in the day but imagine having to put together all those episodes in one season week after week with few breaks. Sure there were some bad ones but so what? Nowadays you get 8-12 episodes, have to wait a year for the next ones, and all of them have to be terrific because if not people will tune out and it will be cancelled—no time to warm up to a show or for it to get its legs. It’s a shame, really, as much as I enjoy streaming and having everything at your fingertips, there was a charm to it.

And that last MASH episode, yes, that really was an event!

